.TH TMUX-CONTINUUM-DEFAULT-SERVER 1 "2026-08-10" "tmux-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tmux-continuum-default-server \- keep persistence ownership on tmux's default server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tmux-continuum-default-server
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tmux-continuum-default-server
coordinates tmux-continuum and tmux-resurrect when multiple tmux servers use
different sockets. It is intended to run from
.B run-shell
after plugins and their options have loaded.
.PP
The command compares the active server socket with
.IR ${TMUX_TMPDIR:-/tmp}/tmux-UID/default .
It canonicalizes both parent directories before comparison, so a symlinked
.B TMUX_TMPDIR
does not prevent the actual default server from being recognized. A socket
with the basename
.I default
in another directory remains isolated.
.PP
For a non-default server, the command replaces tmux-continuum's native
.B status-right
save interpolation with
.BR tmux-continuum-save-gate (1)
using an interval of zero. Status refreshes therefore avoid unnecessary save
work, and that server receives no save or restore ownership.
.PP
For the default server, the command restores Continuum's configured save
interval, publishes a generic automatic-restore signal, repairs the gated save
interpolation, and launches tmux-resurrect once when the server is still new.
The last-save timestamp is initialized before the save interpolation becomes
active, preventing the first status render from racing the restore.
.PP
Missing plugins and unavailable tmux state are treated as advisory activation
failures. The command exits quietly so optional persistence support cannot make
the rest of a tmux configuration unusable.
.SH TMUX OPTIONS
.TP
.B @tmux-tools-continuum-save-interval
Positive save interval, in minutes, to apply on the default server. Missing or
invalid values use 5.
.TP
.B @tmux-tools-resurrect-auto-restore
Published as
.B on
when the default server owns automatic restore. This is the stable signal for
downstream consumers that must coordinate with tmux-resurrect.
.TP
.B @tmux-tools-resurrect-restore-started-at
Internal deduplication marker containing the server start time whose restore
has already been launched. Consumers should not use this option as policy.
.TP
.B @continuum-restore-max-delay
Maximum server age, in seconds, during which fallback restore may start.
Malformed values use 10.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TMUX
Provides the active socket path when present. If absent, the command asks tmux
for
.BR #{socket_path} .
.TP
.B TMUX_TMPDIR
Overrides the parent of tmux's conventional per-user socket directory.
.TP
.B TMUX_PLUGIN_MANAGER_PATH
Root containing the tmux-continuum and tmux-resurrect checkouts. The default is
.IR $HOME/.local/share/tmux-plugins .
.TP
.B HOME
Used for the default plugin root and the restore halt file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/tmux_no_auto_restore
When present, suppresses fallback restore without disabling automatic saving.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Activation completed, was unnecessary, or could not safely proceed.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
set -g @continuum-save-interval 0
set -g @tmux-tools-continuum-save-interval 5
run-shell 'tmux-continuum-default-server'
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tmux (1),
.BR tmux-continuum-save-gate (1)
